Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||05-11-2001||09:27 PM||||Where the heck can you get a decent jack on the South Shore MA?<P>I decided to go to Lappen's in Weymouth. It is brand new, I'm a Power Card member, and it's right by my house. Turns out that it's too new, not even open yet. So, after a short visit to Then and Now Automotive next door (More stuff for my Valiant there, not the Fiero), where my son dropped a bunch of candy on the floor, I decided to knuckle under and go to Auto Zone.<P>Now, I don't like Auto Zone very much, because they woun't sell me an engine. Not that I would buy one from them anyway, but a while ago, I decided to do some preliminary figgerin' as to how much I'd like to spend on my baby. When I asked them about the 3.4 short block, I was told that since the Fiero was never offered with a 3.4, I couldn't obtain one from them. They didn't have 2.8's so, essentially, they didn't have anything for me. Ditto on the jack. "How high do you need to go?" I was asked. "About 20 inches." "How tall are your stands?" "About 14 inches." "So why do you need that height?" You're the expert, I thought. "Because the suspension sags when you lift from the center (Duh)." Anyway, my son threw a fit in AZ when I told him that he couldn't have the eight or so Hot Wheels cars that he'd grabbed. My daughter, of course, was na angel.<P>I ended up going to Sears. They didn't have the nifty 3 1/2 ton jack (On sale for $99.99) so I got the 2 1/2 ton with stands ($89.99). Boy did that suck. Turned a half hour job of getting a Fiero into the air into an hour and a half job of getting the front end up only. The jack wouln't lift at all unless the arm was raised to an almost completely upright position, which couldn't be obtained with the jack at the front center jack point. Needless to say, I retuned this set.<P>Called Summit for their jack (SUM-G1030 $89.99). Backordered three weeks. Sears.com has the jack I want, for $34.00 add'l shipping.<P>I'm just frustrated....||||reg||8
Z||000001||Black88GT||05-11-2001||09:45 PM||||I have that same Sears jack, the 2 1/2 ton jack.  It works fine for me, I can jack the car up and get it on stands in about 10 min.  Not as quick as the bigger jack but I couldn't afford that one.||||reg||1
