Z||000003||LZeitgeist||05-12-2001||01:51 AM||||WTF do they care what kind of car you own? If you want to buy a 3.4, they should sell you a 3.4!!!!!! <P>WTF is wrong with salespeople?!?!?!?!||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||05-12-2001||03:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B><BR>WTF is wrong with salespeople?!?!?!?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WTF is wrong with couriers I reckon. Delays on orders in the USA? I can get a package to any USA state from here in 24 hours on express delivery and 3 days on the slow trip.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000005||thomas_l||05-12-2001||07:10 AM||||Floor jacks are one of those things like a/c gauges or digital volt meters - buy high quality and you never buy another one. It's just having to part with good $$$ up front paying for an immediate need. I haven't looked lately but the 3-1/2 ton Lincoln floor jack I own was bought 10 years ago for around $250. About the only thing I need to do is fill and bleed the hydraulics since it's a little soft at the top of its reach. The side benefit is that its stout enough to roll a car around without tipping over. And I can get my 87 GT up on 4 stands in about 5 min and use it to pivot the car sideways in the front of my garage (when it's not being used for a few days) and leave room for the other two cars indoors.<P>I too have run into businesses that won't work on/sell non-OEM stuff - I just go down the street because they apparently have too much revenue to be bothered with my business. When we were getting my wife's son's 87 Caprice (ex-police car) road ready, I went to a local tire store requesting a smaller size (3 size smaller on the stock rims) for a zero-dollar lowering effect. No dice - they would only do stock or standard dia/offset wheel/tire plus size. No prob. I went down the street to Pep Boys and they gladly took my money and sold me what I asked for. Now that those are worn out he thinks he wants some 20" rims. I say get a job and your rims are down at the store waiting for you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||Patrick's Dad||05-12-2001||07:17 PM||||Thanks guys,<P>Thomas_, I know what you mean. I should just spring $189 for the Snap-On, and my buddy Bill will deliver it. It's just Bill's bill....<P>Yeah, I was really miffed at Auto Zone for the engine debacle. It amounts to not much right now, as I am seriously considering the Short*, and I'll have to get that out of a junker.<P>Still going to try Lappens in Norwood for a jack first.||||reg||1
